    "reasoning": "All 16 final answers agree with the mathematics and their own captured worked solutions. However, q-104803 contains an authored error in its final calculation: an extra -f′(-2) appears after the correct product-rule expression. That displayed expression would equal -2, whereas the correct product-rule result and MA's stated final answer are -3. The answer itself does not disagree. Independent checks: q-114345 projects (3,5) onto 2x+3y=3, giving (3/13,11/13). q-74417 and q-114343 use perpendicular distances 6/√2=3√2 and 8/√2=4√2. q-47449 and q-71524 use negative reciprocals of tangent slopes 3 and 4. q-47410 gives x+10y=71, hence p+q=81. q-104073 has tangent slope 1, so its normal is y=20-x. q-72998 has segment slope -2/3. q-104786 gives -1+2(-1/2)=-2. q-104787 gives 2(-1)-2/3=-8/3. q-104803 gives (-1)(3)+(0)(1/2)=-3. q-15664 gives (1·2-3·(-1))/2²=5/4. q-48952 gives (0·(-1)-1·1)/(-1)²=-1. The two selected scatter plots contain exactly their respective table pairs. q-134085 shows the point (20,6). No submitted-grade evidence is supplied; all MA evidence below comes from each question's captured worked solution.",
